# Line endings.
#
# The repo is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux, so anything the
# server executes must be LF regardless of what the checkout looks like.
# `pim-studio-sync.sh` shipped with CRLF once and failed in a way that read
# like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem:
#
#     set: -: invalid option
#     $'\r': command not found
#     syntax error: unexpected end of file
#
# It is installed by cron, so it failed nightly and silently. The deploy
# script next to it happened to be LF and worked, which made the difference
# look like something specific to the sync.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
